# Documentation PDF stays in sync with content

The header **Download PDF** button must always generate `nimble-construction-accounting-documentation.pdf` from the current [`content/`](content/) markdown and [`public/images/`](public/images/) screenshots. Never replace it with a checked-in copy of the original PDF.

When documentation content changes, the next download must include those changes. Update [`server/utils/documentationPdf.ts`](server/utils/documentationPdf.ts) and [`server/assets/user-guide.css`](server/assets/user-guide.css) if the export pipeline or print layout must change. Preserve the original print layout: A4, cover page with logo, chapter page breaks, screenshot captions, and footer `Nimble Construction Accounting Documentation • {page}`.

Keep sidebar, homepage, import script, and PDF chapter order identical. Chapter files use zero-padded prefixes (`01.` through `09.`, then `10.`–`13.`) plus `navigation.order` so the list never sorts as 1, 10, 11, 2:

1. Foundation and master data
2. Projects
3. Cost codes
4. Item Types and Items List
5. Estimates
6. Purchase Orders
7. Change Orders
8. Stock Receipt Notes (GRN)
9. Vendor Invoices
10. Reports
11. End-to-end workflows
12. Troubleshooting and FAQ
13. Glossary and status reference
